    "notes": "Helper 1.81: the button step Open a menu. A bar button can open any menu in the Helper's list; the Hub editor lists them from the Helper. (Helper 1.80: a list of every menu and pop-up the Helper can open, with the way each one opens (/api/menus, /api/menu/open). The middle button now opens its default menu from that list. A mouse set can open a menu with Run a Helper button on the built-in group Menus. (Helper 1.79: Amit Mouse safety. A mouse that is not the primary one can never be left with no way to left-click: a set that would do that has its Left-button change dropped. (Helper 1.78: Amit Mouse follows the mouse in use. The Helper reports which mouse moved or was pressed last; the page checks that only when it gets focus or is clicked, and checks the background only slowly. (Helper 1.77: dictation follows the focus. While you dictate into a text box it carries on in any other text box you click into, and when you leave every text box while talking the Dictate window opens by itself with what you said. An open Dictate window moves its words into the next text box you click into, closes, and your dictation carries on there. Pressing Enter no longer causes half of an earlier phrase to be typed again. Also carries 1.76 and 1.75 (Helper bar icons centered).))))",
